<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taj Mahal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Taj Mahal is a white marble mausoleum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built by the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> in the seventeenth century in memory of his wife Mumtaz Mahal. Combining Persian, Central Asian and Indian architectural traditions, it is widely regarded as the masterpiece of Mughal architecture. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> profile cites it as part of the empire's enduring cultural legacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taj-mahal.jpg" alt="Taj Mahal" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yann; edited by Jim Carter · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taj_Mahal_(Edited).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
